# The noncentrality argument of Lemma 13.3.14

The completed initial reductions are:
* (a): the contrary centrality assumption places the actual conjugate span
  in Ω₁(Z(Q₁)), with its two generating descriptions identified;
* (b) for the natural L₃(2) branch: V₃=V forces O²(C_G(U))=1;
* (c): the earlier parabolic action gives nontrivial O₂(L₊*) under (a);
  its movement premise is proved for the natural L₃(2) branch.

The L₃(2) application retains the original natural representation and flag.
Its only earlier universal implications are the existing 12.2.2, 1.2.7 and
12.2.13 interfaces. The other helpers expose precisely their local inputs;
these must be established when the complete source theorem is assembled.

Solvability and odd-prime rank in the other branches, Fitting centralization,
component placement, the five-dimensional-module exclusion and the final
diagonal A₅/block chief-factor contradiction remain outstanding. In particular
this module does not yet assert the noncentrality conclusion of 13.3.14.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
Lemma 13.3.14, printed pp.891–893, PDF pp.908–910.
-/
